  "wikipedia_title": "Harlem Renaissance",
  "wikipedia_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Harlem_Renaissance",
  "summary": "The Harlem Renaissance was an intellectual and cultural movement of African-American music, dance, art, fashion, literature, theater, politics, and scholarship centered in Harlem, Manhattan, New York City, spanning the 1920s and 1930s. At the time, it was known as the \"New Negro Movement\", named after The New Negro, a 1925 anthology edited by philosopher Alain Locke, who is regarded as the \"Dean\" of the Harlem Renaissance. The movement also included the new African-American cultural expressions across the urban areas in the Northeastern United States and the Midwestern United States affected by a renewed militancy in the general struggle for civil rights, combined with the Great Migration of African-American workers fleeing the racist conditions of the Jim Crow Deep South, as Harlem was the final destination of the largest number of those who migrated north.",
